# Docs split (agents vs vault)

## Agents

- Read `context.md` first (app root).
- Prefer **code + `supabase/migrations/`** over Markdown when they conflict.
- Do **not** open the whole `vault/` before every task.
- Do not treat the vault as primary agent context.

## Humans / vault updates

Update `vault/` **only** when these change:

- Product decisions / lifecycle / workflow
- Launch checklist / remaining client work
- Domain inventory (listings / portals / related entities)
- Env, alerts, external sync/ToS, how to run

Also update `context.md` for those same facts.

## Do NOT update vault for

- Pure refactors, UI polish, perf tweaks, test-only changes
- Routine API/schema digests already visible in code (Architecture notes refresh rarely, for onboarding humans)

## Do not

- Duplicate long API/schema dumps into notes after every PR
- Put secrets in the vault beyond what’s already needed for local demo ops (names + pointers only)
